    "note": "**Engine-state teaching pass · part 1 — R *consumption* + C *claim*, narrated. Same seed.**\n\nYou said R \"just went from 3 to 0 at the end of the split — didn't explain which frames got it.\" Now the remainder is **handed out tile-by-tile**:\n\n**R counts DOWN as fat tiles claim it.** The split's remainder is computed from geometry, then each emitted tile that's a pixel fatter than the floor **claims one** — R ticks `2 → 1 → 0` (this row) / `3 → 2 → 1 → 0` (the 9-split), pulsing on the tile that took it. It hits 0 *on the claiming frame*, not at the close. (Safety net: any px absorbed by a nested region is reconciled at the close instead of lingering.)\n\n**The narration now reads out the engine moves** (lean into the text layer, as you asked):\n- `Emit tile 6 — …px. Claims 1 leftover remainder px (one of the fat tiles).`\n- `Passthrough — donate 274px forward (carry now 274px), claimed by the next tile.`\n- `Emit tile 3 — …px. Absorbs 274px donated by a passthrough.`\n\n**C is explicit about the claim moment** — a `>` raises C by the donated px, and the *next tile* drives C back to 0 with an \"Absorbs Npx\" callout. A donation is netted out of the remainder math, so the 274px carry is never miscounted as remainder (only the genuine 2 leftover px register).\n\n*(Ruler nudged tighter again, `22 → 18px`. 168 tests green incl. 8 new on R-countdown / carry / no-double-count.)*\n\n**Deferred to part 2 (next candidate):** remove the dashed split overlay once a frame claims its cell · N row/col axis note on the arity field.",
